{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "DeepERC report, schema 1.0",
  "description": "The JSON report one board run writes (steps/step_10_report.py build_report). THE 1.x PROMISE: within 1.x only additive changes are made: new optional keys and new reason codes. A new row status value, or removing, renaming or retyping a covered key, or changing a covered key's meaning, is 2.0. COVERED: schema_version, generated_at, provenance (the key, not its contents), source_netlist, summary, the seven finding arrays, not_checked_parts, not_checked_pins, power_rails_confirmed, and the optional drift_warning and staged_cache_notice. The keys evidence_label, evidence and explanation are covered; their wording is not. NOT COVERED: extraction_metadata, the contents of provenance, rail_candidates, rail_map_conflicts. Every object is open (additionalProperties is not restricted), so a 1.x report with keys added later still validates. ROW STATUS: closed list PASS, WARN, FAIL, UNRESOLVABLE. The key holding it is status on results, power_supply_results, structural_integrity_results and output_conflict_results, and severity on peripheral_integrity_results, pullup_value_results and pullup_presence_results. REASON CODES: upper-snake strings; every code list is open and the known codes are listed in each key's description and x-known-codes. PART NUMBERS: every covered part_number is written with leading and trailing whitespace removed. BOARD VERDICT: not stored in the report. classify_report computes it from the verdict keys above, and the [VERDICT] line, the main.py exit code and the corpus summary.json status carry it. Its frozen vocabulary is all_pass, pass_with_unresolvable, has_warn, has_fail, has_unresolvable_only, no_checkable_nets, pipeline_error; all_pass means no UNRESOLVABLE row. main.py exits non-zero on has_fail (and on a pipeline failure, which writes no report). The rest of summary.json is not part of the 1.0 promise.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^1\\.[0-9]+(?![\\s\\S])",
      "description": "\"1.0\" for this file. Checked by pattern, so a 1.x report validates against the 1.x schema file."
    },
    "generated_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "UTC time the report was written (ISO 8601)."
    },
    "provenance": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Which code, cache and input produced the report. The key is covered; its contents are not."
    },
    "source_netlist": {
      "type": "string"
    },
